5443 true] [17592186529336 1074 "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,2\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,12 v^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,72 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529337 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529366 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529337 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529375 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529337 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529384 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529337 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529392 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529337 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529394 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529337 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535805 175921860454