 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529380 1074 "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3 u + 3 v,\\,3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )},\\,3 u v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u + 3 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u + 3 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,6 v,\\,3 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 3 \\cos{(u )} & 3 v \\\\ 3 & 6 v & 3 u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\cos{(u )} & 3 v \\\\ 6 v & 3 u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 v \\\\ 3 & 3 u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 \\cos{(u )} \\\\ 3 & 6 v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(3 \\cos{(u )})(3 u)-(3 v)(6 v),\\,-[(3)(3 u)-(3 v)(3)],\\,(3)(6 v)-(3 \\cos{(u )})(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9 u \\cos{(u )} - 18 v^{2},\\,- 9 u + 9 v,\\,18 v - 9 \\cos{(u )}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529381 1080 "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩" 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529381 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529381 1083 #uuid "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969" 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529382 1080 "⟨12,\\,- 8 e^{v},\\,-6⟩" 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529382 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529382 1083 #uuid "ac60ce9d-5cfc-5603-8b92-38ff4555d026" 13194139535805 17592186045443 true] [17592186529383 1080 "⟨0,\\,